Subject: [PATCH 3/9] EXEC-MU-ACCOUNTS ultracode re-check C-P1S (Phase 1
 per-user state): four failing probes

- tests/test_c_p1s_preferences_plan.py: /api/v1/preferences reads and writes the Backtest's My conditions (ml.my) and
  the Screener's last screen (scr.last) for a plan that holds neither tab (D5).
- screener/tests/smoke/c_p1s_plan_refused_cache.mjs: the Screener's cached paint (scr.boot + terminal-files, keyed by
  login) still shows the last result's rows after the catalog and the run answer 403 CAPABILITY_REQUIRED (D5).
- terminal/tests/data/c_p1s_drawings_plan.test.ts: a 403 CAPABILITY_REQUIRED on the drawings routes is read as "the
  account cannot be reached": the drawing is kept in the browser and the message names a connection failure.
- terminal/tests/data/c_p1s_browser_keys.test.ts: ml.assets.flow.{collapsed,h}.<TICKER> (class browser) survive
  sign-out and a change of user, naming the tickers the account added as series.

